.SH NAME
Plack::Middleware::Session::Cookie \- Session middleware that saves session data in the cookie
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 5
\&  enable \*(AqSession::Cookie\*(Aq,
\&    session_key => \*(Aqmy_session\*(Aq,
\&    expires     => 3600, # 1 hour
\&    secret      => \*(Aqtop\-secret\*(Aq
\&    ;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This middleware component allows you to use the cookie as a sole
cookie state and store, without any server side storage to do the
session management. This middleware utilizes its own state and store
automatically for you, so you can't override the objects.
.SH CONFIGURATIONS
.IX Header "CONFIGURATIONS"
This middleware is a subclass of Plack::Middleware::Session and
accepts most configuration of the parent class. In addition, following
options are accepted.
.IP secret 4
.IX Item "secret"
Server side secret to sign the session data using HMAC SHA1. Defaults
to nothing (i.e. do not sign) but \fBstrongly recommended\fR to set your
own secret string.
.Sp
Unless you use your own serializer/deserializer, running this
middleware without setting a secret is vulnerable to arbitrary code
execution. \fBIn the future release it will be required to set the
secret\fR.
.IP "session_key, domain, expires, path, secure, httponly, samesite" 4
.IX Item "session_key, domain, expires, path, secure, httponly, samesite"
Accessors for the cookie attributes. See
Plack::Session::State::Cookie for these options.
.SH AUTHOR
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
Tatsuhiko Miyagawa
